sources/build materials are included in heic-sources.zip. See HEIC-NOTICE.

WebP: libwebp 1.6.0 (4fa21912338357f89e4fd51cf2368325b59e9bd9), BSD-3-Clause
and its additional patent grant. See modern-webp-COPYING, PATENTS and AUTHORS.
The build includes libsharpyuv under the same terms. Lossless encoding preserves
all RGBA input samples (exact=1), including RGB behind fully transparent pixels.

JPEG XL: libjxl 0.12.0 (a7a9c787341cf703dede03c2009fa460cae5e5df), BSD-3-Clause
and additional patent grant. See modern-jxl-LICENSE, PATENTS and AUTHORS.
Build scripts bearing Apache-2.0 headers retain that license (Apache-2.0-LICENSE).
Pinned upstream submodules: Brotli 028fb5a (MIT), Highway 457c891
(Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause, both texts supplied), skcms 96d9171 (BSD-3-Clause).
Only these dependencies are linked. No sjpeg, lcms, libpng, JPEGli, OpenEXR,
test fixtures, HEVC reference software or external network loading is included.
The wrapper handles the first displayed frame in RGBA8. Lossless applies to
these input samples, not to metadata, animation, HDR or prior canvas conversions.

Build provenance: sources/modern/sources.lock.json pins upstream URLs, commits,
original archive SHA-256 and selected-source SHA-256. The upstream archives are
unmodified. The project appends its MIT block-map.inc extension to the extracted
libjxl decoder during the build and provides its own bridge.cpp and offline build.py. The selected
archives omit image fixtures and unused dependencies. CMake/Ninja/Python and
the portable Emscripten SDK are build tools, not included application scripts.

Both modules use Emscripten 6.0.9: Emscripten/MIT-or-NCSA glue and emmalloc,
musl permissive notices, libc++/libc++abi/compiler-rt/LLVM libc under
Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception and retained legacy terms. Their full texts and
credits are already supplied: Emscripten-LICENSE, Emscripten-AUTHORS,
musl-COPYRIGHT, libcxx-LICENSE, libcxxabi-LICENSE, compiler-rt-LICENSE,
compiler-rt-CREDITS and llvm-libc-LICENSE. No external filesystem is used.

